<content>
    <sensor>
        <name>CUST - System Disk Space</name>
        <what_hash>2714975505</what_hash>
        <category>Miscellaneous</category>
        <description>Sensor to get the system disk space.

Data returned is unified in integer and can be used to filter.

Using : shutil.disk_usage(path)
Return disk usage statistics about the given path as a named tuple with the attributes total, used and free, which are the amount of total, used and free space, in bytes. path may be a file or a directory.</description>
        <result_type>1</result_type>
        <qseconds>900</qseconds>
        <ignore_case_flag>1</ignore_case_flag>
        <delimiter>|</delimiter>
        <hidden_flag>0</hidden_flag>
        <queries>
            <sensor_query>
                <sensor_type>8</sensor_type>
                <os>0</os>
                <query>import shutil
import tanium

total, used, free = shutil.disk_usage(&quot;&#x2F;&quot;)

tanium.results.add(str((total &#x2F;&#x2F; (2**30)))+&quot;|&quot;+str((used &#x2F;&#x2F; (2**30)))+&quot;|&quot;+str((free &#x2F;&#x2F; (2**30))))
</query>
